{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For therefore have you passed by your servant.</b> For the sake of this — that you eat a little — you have passed by me, for it is not the way of wayfarers to fast, and now it is midday; but I recognize in you that you are modest and bashful." "<b>So shall you do, as you have said.</b> What you said: 'and I will fetch a morsel of bread.' That is, if you wish us to eat with you, prepare a small thing. Nevertheless, do not refrain from preparing a large meal, for so is the way of important people when they invite their fellows to eat with them. Another interpretation: <b>so shall you do</b> — may it be HaShem's will that you manage to do thus forever, just as you now volunteer to host guests."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:36.470497254Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}